    "body": "Fixes #2527\n\nWhen Borg reports an error such as a permission failure, Vorta can receive both a readable error message and the full Python traceback. Since the status bar always displays the latest message, the traceback was shown there and usually got cut off due to its length.\n\nThis PR adds a small helper to extract the actual exception from Borg traceback messages. The shortened message is now used by the status bar and the job error list, while the complete traceback is still written to the log for debugging.\n\nThis also handles chained exceptions, Borg's appended system information, and errors coming from remote repositories. Normal messages are left unchanged.\n\nAdded tests covering:\n\n- Simple and chained Python tracebacks\n- Borg-style traceback output with system information\n- Permission errors shown by a Borg job\n\nRuff and mypy pass, and the full CI suite passes across Python 3.10, 3.12 and 3.13, Ubuntu/macOS, and Borg 1.2.8/1.4.4.\n\nThe Jobs page reason column still reports these cases as Local Exception, which can be addressed separately.\n",
